{
  "headline": "Haloperidol lactate is not on FDA's shortage list; Corvale East has 5.3 days of 5 mg/mL vials and Corvale General can spare 30 vials while keeping 14 days",
  "headline_cites": ["D7", "D1", "D2", "D8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list shows haloperidol lactate is not listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 40 vials of the 5 mg/mL 1 mL presentation at 7.6 vials per day, giving 5.3 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 140 vials of the same presentation at 7.8 vials per day, giving 17.9 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked option 1 is to transfer 30 vials from Corvale General to Corvale East; after transfer Corvale General would retain 14 days and Corvale East would reach 9 days.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "All three sites' 5 mg/mL vials carry NDC 55154955305 and are labeled by Cardinal Health 107, LLC with SPL set ID e2eed126, which names Fresenius Kabi USA as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E5", "E6", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A separate FDA shortage entry shows Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC plans to discontinue haloperidol decanoate injection (not the lactate formulation) with an initial posting date of 2026-01-09.",
      "cites": ["E25"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No FDA inspection or enforcement action is recorded for the Fresenius Kabi USA plant linked to this NDC in the provided evidence.",
      "cites": ["E7"]
    }
  ]
}
